WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.503
- This looks like the
best taste test ever,

00:00:01.503 --> 00:00:03.129
cause they just asked
what my favorite food was

00:00:03.129 --> 00:00:03.964
and I told them,

00:00:03.964 --> 00:00:05.724
and now I got it.

00:00:07.970 --> 00:00:09.264
What the (bleep) is that?

00:00:09.264 --> 00:00:14.146
(heavy instrumental music)

00:00:17.855 --> 00:00:20.281
- I've got ramen, fresh fruit, horchata.

00:00:20.281 --> 00:00:22.197
(bleep) fusion, bruh.

00:00:22.197 --> 00:00:24.403
This actually might not be that bad.

00:00:24.403 --> 00:00:26.493
"Ramchata," it's a "ramchata."

00:00:26.493 --> 00:00:29.198
Ramen and horchata together at last.

00:00:29.198 --> 00:00:30.162
Get in there.

00:00:30.162 --> 00:00:31.822
Smells delicious.

00:00:31.822 --> 00:00:34.504
I'm blaming the strawberries
and the peaches.

00:00:34.504 --> 00:00:36.779
Is it weird how excited I am about this?

00:00:36.779 --> 00:00:38.463
I think this is gonna
actually taste great.

00:00:38.463 --> 00:00:38.993
Let's see.

00:00:38.993 --> 00:00:42.511
(heavy instrumental music)

00:00:42.511 --> 00:00:43.752
No.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:45.507
(coughs)

00:00:45.507 --> 00:00:47.260
There's little chunks
of mealy ramen in here.

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:48.723
(bleep) devil's cocktail.

00:00:48.723 --> 00:00:50.267
Nine different things stuck
in my teeth right now.

00:00:50.267 --> 00:00:52.554
That's the grossest
combination you can make.

00:00:52.554 --> 00:00:53.808
It smells so good though.

00:00:53.808 --> 00:00:56.511
- It just smells like donuts and cheese.

00:00:56.511 --> 00:00:58.649
Why are you doing this to me?

00:00:58.649 --> 00:01:02.237
(blending)

00:01:02.237 --> 00:01:03.932
That's a terrible color.

00:01:03.932 --> 00:01:06.323
The chips don't really blend well.

00:01:06.323 --> 00:01:10.448
It's kind of just like a
bunch of soggy chip crumbs.

00:01:11.533 --> 00:01:14.331
Surprisingly, not that disgusting.

00:01:14.331 --> 00:01:17.129
Kinda sweet and light and not that bad.

00:01:17.129 --> 00:01:18.464
I'm blown away.

00:01:18.464 --> 00:01:21.262
The burnt TV dinner,
that's what we'll call it.

00:01:21.262 --> 00:01:22.841
Cause that's what it tastes like.

00:01:22.841 --> 00:01:23.909
I mean, I wouldn't make it,

00:01:23.909 --> 00:01:26.347
cause why would I put
these things in a shake?

00:01:26.347 --> 00:01:27.926
- Mashed potatoes, beer, chicken,

00:01:27.926 --> 00:01:30.144
shrimp and cocktail sauce.

00:01:30.144 --> 00:01:31.804
None of this is gonna be good.

00:01:31.804 --> 00:01:33.847
Everybody knows, once you vomit a food,

00:01:33.847 --> 00:01:35.472
you never want to eat that food again.

00:01:35.472 --> 00:01:37.063
This is gonna taste like vomit.

00:01:37.063 --> 00:01:38.642
I don't want this to ruin my life.

00:01:38.642 --> 00:01:40.024
Let's do it.

00:01:40.024 --> 00:01:41.150
(blending)

00:01:41.150 --> 00:01:42.264
This is as white as me.

00:01:42.264 --> 00:01:44.533
It smells like, um.

00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:48.198
(gagging)

00:01:48.198 --> 00:01:50.578
A little bit like a chowder.

00:01:50.578 --> 00:01:51.867
I was trying to keep it under my tongue

00:01:51.867 --> 00:01:52.772
so I didn't taste it.

00:01:52.772 --> 00:01:53.910
It moves like wet sand.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:54.827
The more I smell it,

00:01:54.827 --> 00:01:56.035
the less I'm revolted by it.

00:01:56.035 --> 00:01:56.952
Now I'm starting to think

00:01:56.952 --> 00:01:58.368
I would like it if it was warm.

00:01:58.368 --> 00:02:00.328
(beep)

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:02.046
Almost palatable.

00:02:02.046 --> 00:02:03.091
- We got some brie.

00:02:03.091 --> 00:02:04.635
Some sweet potato, which I love.

00:02:04.635 --> 00:02:05.506
Broccoli.

00:02:05.506 --> 00:02:06.628
Kale.

00:02:08.008 --> 00:02:09.970
This one might be good without the cheese.

00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:14.970
(blending and screaming)

00:02:16.019 --> 00:02:17.296
It's real bad.

00:02:17.296 --> 00:02:19.851
First of all, it's warm from the tea.

00:02:19.851 --> 00:02:21.023
These little guys on the broccoli,

00:02:21.023 --> 00:02:21.859
they don't blend.

00:02:21.859 --> 00:02:23.113
And then the cheese comes in again.

00:02:23.113 --> 00:02:25.316
It's turning back to solid.

00:02:26.358 --> 00:02:27.821
This is vomit.

00:02:27.821 --> 00:02:29.769
I think the name for it is vomit.

00:02:29.769 --> 00:02:31.281
- In theory, it should
taste like awesomeness.

00:02:31.281 --> 00:02:33.567
But, I don't know.

00:02:33.567 --> 00:02:34.741
Let me talk myself.

00:02:34.741 --> 00:02:36.749
Do it, do it.

00:02:36.749 --> 00:02:38.836
(blending)

00:02:38.836 --> 00:02:40.462
Everything that has artificial pizza

00:02:40.462 --> 00:02:41.704
has like one smell,

00:02:41.704 --> 00:02:44.072
and it has that same smell.

00:02:44.072 --> 00:02:46.174
In honor of it looking like baby food,

00:02:46.174 --> 00:02:47.159
I'm gonna airplane it.

00:02:47.159 --> 00:02:48.828
(airplane motor)

00:02:48.828 --> 00:02:49.712
I'm so scared.

00:02:49.712 --> 00:02:50.594
I'm so scared.

00:02:50.594 --> 00:02:51.384
I'm terrified.

00:02:51.384 --> 00:02:54.426
You've put much weirder
things in your mouth before.

00:02:57.084 --> 00:02:58.350
That's actually really good.

00:02:58.350 --> 00:02:59.441
A pizza smoothie.

00:02:59.441 --> 00:03:00.927
This here, this is eatin'.

00:03:00.927 --> 00:03:01.937
If it was warmed up, I'm telling you,

00:03:01.937 --> 00:03:02.901
I would take this all down.

00:03:02.901 --> 00:03:04.445
It's like baby food.

00:03:04.445 --> 00:03:05.652
(train)

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:06.488
If you want your baby to have

00:03:06.488 --> 00:03:07.982
childhood diabetes.

00:03:07.982 --> 00:03:12.982
(blending)

00:03:13.904 --> 00:03:14.821
Can I take this?

00:03:14.821 --> 00:03:15.955
This is not bad.

00:03:15.955 --> 00:03:17.831
This is not bad.

